From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Ziliani <rylos78@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:32:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] libcamera: camera_lens: Close the lens subdev when not
 in use

Lens drivers such as dw9714, dw9719 and ak7375 power the lens up when
the subdev is opened and down when it is closed. On ACPI platforms
ipu-bridge also adds a runtime PM device link from the lens to its
camera sensor, so an open lens subdev keeps the sensor powered too.

CameraLens opens the subdev in init() and keeps it open for the lifetime
of the CameraManager. With a long-lived camera manager, such as the
WirePlumber libcamera monitor, the lens and the sensor are then never
powered down, even when no camera is in use.

Close the subdev at the end of init(), once the lens driver has been
validated and the controls have been cached, and add open() and close()
functions that pipeline handlers can use to power the lens for the
duration of a capture session. setFocusPosition() reopens the subdev on
demand, so pipeline handlers that don't call open() keep working as
before, the lens being powered from the first focus change on.

Signed-off-by: Marco Ziliani <rylos78@gmail.com>
---
 include/libcamera/internal/camera_lens.h |  2 ++
 src/libcamera/camera_lens.cpp            | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/libcamera/internal/camera_lens.h b/include/libcamera/internal/camera_lens.h
index f347c5e0..f63bcfa2 100644
--- a/include/libcamera/internal/camera_lens.h
+++ b/include/libcamera/internal/camera_lens.h
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ public:
 	~CameraLens();
 
 	int init();
+	int open();
+	void close();
 	int setFocusPosition(int32_t position);
 
 	const std::string &model() const { return model_; }
diff --git a/src/libcamera/camera_lens.cpp b/src/libcamera/camera_lens.cpp
index ccc2a6a6..7be5bfd2 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/camera_lens.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/camera_lens.cpp
@@ -73,9 +73,47 @@ int CameraLens::init()
 		return ret;
 
 	model_ = subdev_->model();
+
+	/*
+	 * Lens drivers commonly keep the lens powered for as long as the
+	 * subdev is open, and the lens power often depends on the camera
+	 * sensor (e.g. through a runtime PM device link). Close the subdev
+	 * until the lens is actually used, so that a long-lived camera
+	 * manager doesn't keep the lens and the sensor powered.
+	 */
+	subdev_->close();
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/**
+ * \brief Open the lens subdev
+ *
+ * Pipeline handlers call this function when the camera starts, to power the
+ * lens for the duration of the capture session. The subdev is also opened on
+ * demand by setFocusPosition().
+ *
+ * \return 0 on success or a negative error code otherwise
+ */
+int CameraLens::open()
+{
+	if (subdev_->isOpen())
+		return 0;
+
+	return subdev_->open();
+}
+
+/**
+ * \brief Close the lens subdev
+ *
+ * Pipeline handlers call this function when the camera stops, to let the lens
+ * driver power the lens down.
+ */
+void CameraLens::close()
+{
+	subdev_->close();
+}
+
 /**
  * \brief This function sets the focal point of the lens to a specific position.
  * \param[in] position The focal point of the lens
@@ -86,6 +124,10 @@ int CameraLens::init()
  */
 int CameraLens::setFocusPosition(int32_t position)
 {
+	int ret = open();
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ControlList lensCtrls(subdev_->controls());
 	lensCtrls.set(V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE, static_cast<int32_t>(position));
 
